{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01293",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.62,
      "end_seconds": 6.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Hmm, doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.36,
      "end_seconds": 11.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.78,
      "end_seconds": 16.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "good morning, doctor. I came along to help out"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.44,
      "end_seconds": 22.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.45,
      "end_seconds": 28.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "It's a high fever with shaking chills, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.32,
      "end_seconds": 31.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 33.1,
      "end_seconds": 38.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Ah, it's febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.5,
      "end_seconds": 56.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.61,
      "end_seconds": 60.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "I'd say two weeks, um, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 62.02,
      "end_seconds": 65.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "It was closer to three weeks, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.56,
      "end_seconds": 71.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.67,
      "end_seconds": 75.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "That sounds about right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.01,
      "end_seconds": 82.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.61,
      "end_seconds": 97.18,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "Actually, honestly, a couple of times a week. Paracetamol helps a bit. I've been sweating a lot too, for one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.85,
      "end_seconds": 99.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "how frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.41,
      "end_seconds": 104.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "It It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.34,
      "end_seconds": 112.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "have you had a high fever with shaking chills before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.21,
      "end_seconds": 123.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "ah, I had a similar thing about six months ago. It went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.48,
      "end_seconds": 131.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "let me check a few things any rash, neck stiffness or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.47,
      "end_seconds": 135.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "actually, none of those, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.46,
      "end_seconds": 143.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Have you had any yellow eyes or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.12,
      "end_seconds": 149.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Oh, no, no yellow eyes or cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.18,
      "end_seconds": 154.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Okay, has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.15,
      "end_seconds": 159.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "I mean, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.11,
      "end_seconds": 163.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.32,
      "end_seconds": 165.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.49,
      "end_seconds": 172.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.01,
      "end_seconds": 176.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Hmm, no allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.47,
      "end_seconds": 180.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.92,
      "end_seconds": 195.22,
      "duration_seconds": 14.3,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. My husband and I live above the shop. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.65,
      "end_seconds": 199.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.37,
      "end_seconds": 211.49,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had gout for five years now. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.69,
      "end_seconds": 224.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.34,
      "end_seconds": 228.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.93,
      "end_seconds": 231.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "let me take your readings now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.12,
      "end_seconds": 244.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "That's it, just a a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.44,
      "end_seconds": 268.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "okay: BP is 119 over 77, temperature 39.3, pulse 104."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.13,
      "end_seconds": 271.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.43,
      "end_seconds": 279.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.54,
      "end_seconds": 303.06,
      "duration_seconds": 11.52,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: I'd lean towards a fever after travel that must be treated as possible malaria. Dengue fever is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.65,
      "end_seconds": 307.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.21,
      "end_seconds": 326.93,
      "duration_seconds": 18.72,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a fever after travel that must be treated as possible malaria, and we'll know more once the a malaria test is back. Let's get a malaria test, for fever after travel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.81,
      "end_seconds": 330.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.66,
      "end_seconds": 343.07,
      "duration_seconds": 11.41,
      "text": "Blood tests is what I'd like next, for fever. Avoid anti-inflammatory painkillers and keep drinking. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.45,
      "end_seconds": 348.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "well, great, thank you for your help"
    }
  ]
}